<title>FRANCE: Usinor Q1 sales fell to 18.4 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Usinor Q1 sales fell to 18.4 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover				     18,423    vs   18,734</p>
<p>- of which</p>
<p>    Flat products				 9,026    vs    8,749</p>
<p>    Stainless steel and alloys		4,095    vs    4,597</p>
<p>    Special steels				3,647    vs    3,896</p>
<p>    Other businesses			    2,274    vs    2,319</p>
<p>    Sales of assets within the group	 -619    vs     -827</p>
<p>NOTE: Usinor gave the figures in a statement. Data for the first quarter of 1996 were restated to take into account the transfer of Sogerail to the flat steels branch. At comparable structure sales fell 2.2 percent.</p>
<p>Current order book levels lead the group to expect for the second quarter of 1997 a sharp rise in volumes in all its businesses over the second quarter of 1996, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
